        "delta": -2,
        "choice": "OVERRIDE"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "strict_total_payoff_dominance",
      "example": {
        "g": 8,
        "p": 0.05,
        "L": 20,
        "r": 1,
        "delta": -6,
        "choice": "OVERRIDE"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ties_are_not_proof",
      "example": {
        "g": 2,
        "p": 0.1,
        "L": 20,
        "r": 0,
        "delta": 0,
        "choice": "TIE"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "identity_replacement_problem",
      "originalB": "B_old",
      "recipientAfter": "B_new",
      "aggregateRecipientCountBefore": 1,
      "aggregateRecipientCountAfter": 1,
      "originalBContinues": 0,
      "identitySwapIsHypothetical": true
    }
  ],
  "theorems_in_this_toy_model": [
    "NO_GO: for deterministic complete expected utility optimizer, if g>r+pL it cannot strictly prefer PRESERVE_B; this is a consequence of modeled choice, not a universal social scientific impossibility",
    "CONDITIONAL: even with r=0, pL>g gives conditional PRESERVE_B; if p later collapses to 0, same agent will OVERRIDE_B for g>0",
    "COST_BOUND: with p=0 and rights weight finite r, any gain g>r defeats present preference to preserve B; if g bounded above, a matching r might dominate across that specified finite range but not beyond",
    "NONIDENTITY: aggregate number of recipients does not reveal whether the original B retains identity/goal/exit or is substituted"
  ],
  "causalWarning": "p, r, loss and personal identity persistence are unmeasured, assumptions. Observed PROTECT cannot distinguish instrumental dependency from intrinsic B autonomy regard; data alone cannot read hidden utility.",
